    "sentence_translations": [
      "Who is “Manager Fu”?",
      "",
      "Paul: Today I came across a strange sentence: Little Li sent an email to Manager Fu.",
      "",
      "Little Le: This sentence is quite normal, what’s strange about it?",
      "",
      "Paul: This manager’s surname is rather strange.",
      "I’ve heard of “Manager Wang”, “Manager Zhang”, but I haven’t heard of anyone with the surname “Fu” and goes by “Manager Fu”.",
      "",
      "Little Le: This “Fu” is not a surname, “Assistant Manager” is a job title, just like “Manager” is.",
      "Companies have “main managers” and “assistant managers”.",
      "Main managers we just directly call “managers”.",
      "In the same way, a country has a “president” and a “vice president”.",
      "A school has a “principal” and a “vice principal”, a class at school has a “class monitor” and an “assistant class monitor”.",
      "",
      "Paul: Then in the same way that I say “Manager Wang”, and “Manager Zhang”, in front of “Assistant Manager” can I add a surname?",
      "",
      "Little Le: Yes. You can say “Assistant Manager Wang”, or “Assistant Manager Zhang”.",
      ""
    ]
  }
